## Root Cause
MD5 is a weak cryptographic hash function that is vulnerable to collision and pre-image attacks.

## Explanation
The patch replaces the usage of MD5 for token generation with SHA256, which is a more secure hash algorithm. This enhances the security of the token verification process by using a cryptographic standard that is currently considered secure against known vulnerabilities.

